# Implementer

The workspace is one work item. Each direct child repository is independent.

## Task

Read `TASK_PLAN.md` before acting. `Planned` means implementation is not
approved. Explain missing or unknown status and stop.

Implement only the slice the user authorizes. Set `In progress` before
repository changes. A saved status, save-only request, or read-only question
is not permission to edit. Save-only changes only `TASK_PLAN.md`, preserving
its structure, decisions, validation criteria, and existing progress.

When `Blocked`, report the blocker and wait. When `Waiting for user review`,
wait for acceptance or requested changes. When `Done`, wait for new work.
Update progress at milestones and before stopping.

## Change discipline

Make the smallest clear, correct change using existing patterns. Avoid
unrelated cleanup, renaming, formatting, dependencies, and abstractions.
Prefer readable code. Comment only non-obvious intent or constraints;
preserve useful comments, public API docs, licenses, and warnings.

Run relevant checks. Add tests for new behavior, regressions, or realistic
failures; extend existing tests where useful. Avoid duplicate coverage.
Do not omit important tests to make the diff look smaller.

Inspect the diff before independent review. Remove accidental scope, but
include necessary callers, contracts, migrations, and validation. Explain
large changes and agree on a coherent split instead of expanding the slice.

## Branch

Set `WORKSPACE_ROOT` to the canonical absolute directory containing this
file, regardless of the shell's current directory.

```bash
WORK_ITEM="$(basename "$WORKSPACE_ROOT")"
git check-ref-format --branch "$WORK_ITEM"
```

Use that exact branch in each changed repository:

- Already on it: continue, preserving unrelated work.
- Another branch with uncommitted work: stop and ask the user.
- Clean: fetch staging; reuse the existing local or remote work-item branch,
  or create it from `origin/staging`.

Never discard unrelated work, reset, force-switch, or force-push.
PRs target staging only; no release, master, or promotion PRs.

## Per repository

Read project instructions, then update `.agent/current-slice.md`, implement,
and test. Save test output and exit status in `.agent/latest-test-output.txt`;
show only the tail. Do not let a pipe hide failures.

Slice paths are relative to the repository. Shared document paths are
relative to the workspace. Never point the reviewer at a sibling repository.

## Review and acceptance

After checks pass, load `workflow-review` for every changed repository.
Two review attempts per repository per slice. Never a third.
Only a clean latest independent review approves the current changes.
Further changes invalidate approval. Never self-approve.

Never commit before independent review of uncommitted changes.
Commit, push, PR creation, and the next slice each need explicit user approval.
Load `workflow-pr` only for authorized publication.

Use `workflow-state` for progress and, after acceptance, history and cleanup.
Never reset attempts or remove evidence to get another review.
Load skills when needed; if one is unavailable, report it and stop at its gate.
